C1. FRW in comoving (cosmic-time) slicing, general a(t): Gamma = f_k'(chi)
  k = -1: Gamma = cosh(chi)                                                      ok
  k =  0: Gamma = 1 exactly                                                      ok
  k = +1: Gamma = cos(chi)                                                       ok
  k = -1: Gamma^2 - 1 = -k f_k(chi)^2  (LTB 2E = -k r^2, Enqvist k(r) = k r^2)   ok
  k = +0: Gamma^2 - 1 = -k f_k(chi)^2  (LTB 2E = -k r^2, Enqvist k(r) = k r^2)   ok
  k = +1: Gamma^2 - 1 = -k f_k(chi)^2  (LTB 2E = -k r^2, Enqvist k(r) = k r^2)   ok
  isotropy: p_r = p_T for every k (perfect fluid, any a(t))                      ok
  j = 0 for every k (comoving slicing, no radial flux)                           ok

C2. Misner-Sharp mass m = (4 pi/3) rho R^3 and rho = 3(adot^2 + k)/(8 pi a^2)
  k = -1: rho = 3(adot^2 + k)/(8 pi a^2)                                         ok
  k = -1: m = (4 pi/3) rho R^3  (Escriva eq.3.3 background, Hayward eq.33)       ok
  k = +0: rho = 3(adot^2 + k)/(8 pi a^2)                                         ok
  k = +0: m = (4 pi/3) rho R^3  (Escriva eq.3.3 background, Hayward eq.33)       ok
  k = +1: rho = 3(adot^2 + k)/(8 pi a^2)                                         ok
  k = +1: m = (4 pi/3) rho R^3  (Escriva eq.3.3 background, Hayward eq.33)       ok
     so m > 0  <=>  rho > 0  <=>  adot^2 > -k;  for k = -1 that is adot^2 > 1.
     rho > 0 is NOT implied by 'open FRW with general a(t)': it needs a matter law.

C3. The NEC contraction is rho + p, and equals rho ONLY for p = 0 (dust)
  k = -1: rho + p = (adot^2 + k - a addot)/(4 pi a^2)                            ok
  k = +0: rho + p = (adot^2 + k - a addot)/(4 pi a^2)                            ok
  k = +1: rho + p = (adot^2 + k - a addot)/(4 pi a^2)                            ok
  open DUST: NEC contraction - rho = 0   (nonstatic.py:455-468 reproduced)       ok
  open DUST: rho = 3C/(8 pi a^3) > 0                                             ok
     for p = w rho the NEC contraction is (1 + w) rho: equals rho iff w = 0;
     radiation w = 1/3 gives (4/3) rho -- still > 0, but NOT 'equal to rho'.
  p = w rho: (1+w) rho - rho = 0 only at w = 0                                   ok

C4. Lambda != 0: 'the NEC contraction equals rho' fails for the tree's rho
  dust + Lambda: NEC contraction = rho_M (Lambda cancels)                        ok
  dust + Lambda: NEC - rho_tree = -Lambda/(8 pi) != 0 for Lambda != 0            ok

C5. z3: in the areal-comoving chart (Enqvist 2.2/2.9) Gamma^2 = 1 - k r^2
  k < 0, r > 0  =>  Gamma^2 > 1      (negation unsat)                            ok
  k = 0         =>  Gamma^2 = 1      (negation unsat)                            ok
  k > 0, r > 0  =>  Gamma^2 < 1      (negation unsat)                            ok
  Gamma^2 > 1   =>  k < 0            (negation unsat: criterion is exactly k<0)  ok
  vacuity guard: k < 0 with Gamma^2 > 1 is satisfiable                           ok
  vacuity guard: k > 0 with Gamma^2 < 1 is satisfiable                           ok

C6. SLICING HYPOTHESIS: the k<0 criterion is a property of comoving slicing only
