     flat dust a=1, adot=2/3, chi=0.3: comoving Gamma = 1, U = 0.200000000; eta = -0.5 -> Gamma' = 1.231845026
  flat FRW, tilted slicing (eta=-0.5): Gamma' > 1 (flat FRW DOES contract there) ok
  z3: untrapped, m > 0  =>  the U'=0 slicing has Gamma'^2 = 1-2m/R < 1 (negation unsat) ok
  vacuity guard: untrapped, m>0 AND comoving Gamma>1 is satisfiable (open FRW exists) ok

